// Brewin' and Chewin' in a real client: water keeps its grade through the keg's buckets and bottles,
// a keg refuses a second grade, a plain bottle still tops up a plain keg, a drawn bottle is cookable, sea
// water comes back out salty, and a broken keg keeps its water's grade; a graded or salty bottle goes
// in, and nothing ferments from sea water while any fresh water brews beer with no grade. It runs on
// the two nodes with the integration, 1.21.1 and 1.21.1-neoforge. The screenshots it leaves in
// run/<node>/agent/client/screenshots/ show Jade's line under a Dirty keg and a salty one. Run it
// unattended in a singleplayer world:
//     ./gradlew ":<node>:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/integrations/brewin-and-chewin.jsonl -Pquickplay=BrewinAgent
// BrewinAgent is a throwaway world, made fresh for each run by
//     python tools/agent/new_world.py <node> BrewinAgent
// Then check what it recorded:
//     python tools/agent/drive.py run/<node>/agent/client tools/agent/integrations/brewin-and-chewin.jsonl --verify --max-age 15
//
// A keg is filled or emptied by right clicking it with the container in hand, which goes through
// KegBlockEntity.extractInWorld. The player stands on it and looks straight down, as in
// kaleidoscope-cookery.jsonl.
//
// The tank is saved differently by the two loaders (a Fabric FluidVariant under "variant", a NeoForge
// FluidStack under "Fluid", in droplets or millibuckets), so the tank is checked by what "data get"
// prints rather than by path. The grade is one component on the fluid: water_purity 0 to 3, or
// water_salty for sea water.
//
// On 1.21.1-neoforge runClient also loads Create, whose bottle handler would take a water bottle into
// the keg as create:potion; the keg's own bottle recipe matches first, graded bottle or not.
//
// Beer takes 9600 ticks, so the fermenting cases run them with server.sprint, which answers as soon
// as the server has: the whole script takes a minute or two on top of the game's start.

{"id": "load", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 400}}
{"id": "arrived", "command": "client.state"}
{"id": "survival", "command": "server.command", "args": {"command": "gamemode survival @p"}}
